# Context budget rules

goclaw targets **qwen2.5-coder:7b** (~8K–32K effective context). Every system prompt injection has a mandatory cap.

## Current caps (do not exceed without a design decision)

| Source | Cap | Enforcement |
|--------|-----|-------------|
| Skills snippet | `cfg.EffectiveSkillsMaxRunes()` default **8 000** | `chat_wiring.go` → `skills.Collect` |
| Each memory block | **4 096 bytes** (`memoryMaxBytes`) | `request.go` `truncateMemoryBlock` |
| Memory entries per store | `cfg.EffectiveMaxMemorySnippetEntries()` default **4** | `request.go` `RelevantContext` |
| Plan body (multi-step) | **30 lines** (`planBodyReferenceMaxLines`) | `planfile/step_execution.go` |
| CLAUDE.md lines | default **60**, hard max **200** | `projectcontext/context.go` |
| Standing orders | default **40**, hard max **120** | `projectcontext/context.go` |
| MCP tool descriptions | **220 runes** | `mcp/adapter.go` |

## Required for any new injection

1. Add an explicit cap — use `text.TruncateRunes`, `truncateLines`, or `truncateMemoryBlock`.
2. Expose the cap via `cfg.EffectiveXxx()` if users should be able to tune it.
3. Append a truncation note: `"\n…(truncated after N — full content at <path>)"`.
4. Never inject raw file content, full plan bodies, or unlimited lists.

## Priority when total is too large (high → low)

Static system prompt → profile overrides → project context → skills → user memory → project memory → todo list → hints

## Anti-patterns

```go
// WRONG — uncapped injection
sys += "\n## Context\n" + rawFileContent

// WRONG — hard-coded limit at call site
skills.Collect(roots, 24000)

// CORRECT
block = truncateMemoryBlock(block, memoryMaxBytes)
sys += "\n\n## Memory\n" + block
```
